---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "Professional Dog Behaviorist San Jacinto | Good Doggos";
const description = "Expert dog behaviorist in San Jacinto. We handle severe aggression, anxiety, and psychological issues using a balanced approach and canine psychology.";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Dog Behaviorist",
  "description": description,
  "provider": {
    "@type": "LocalBusiness",
    "name": "Good Doggos",
    "url": "https://gooddoggos.com",
    "telephone": "+19514016252",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "addressLocality": "San Jacinto",
      "addressRegion": "CA",
      "addressCountry": "US"
    }
  },
  "areaServed": {
    "@type": "AdministrativeArea",
    "name": "Riverside County"
  },
  "url": "https://gooddoggos.com/services/dog-behaviorist"
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Hero Band -->
  <section class="bg-primary-navy pt-32 pb-16 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-body text-white/50 mt-6 mb-4" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Home</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <a href="/services/behavioral-modification" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Behavioral Modification</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <span class="text-white/80 truncate">Dog Behaviorist</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-heading font-bold text-white leading-tight mb-6">
        Expert Dog Behaviorist in San Jacinto
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Body Content -->
  <section class="py-16 px-4 bg-[#FCF9FA]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
      
      <!-- Main Content -->
      <div class="prose max-w-none">
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          If you’re searching for a "dog behaviorist," you’ve likely hit a wall. Maybe your dog’s aggression has escalated to where you’re afraid to have guests in your San Jacinto home, or their separation anxiety is tearing your house apart.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          These psychological issues are symptoms of a mindset that needs to shift from chaos to calm. Because we are professionals, we do not guess or give out generic advice. We must evaluate your dog in person to find the "why" behind the behavior—whether it's fear, dominance, or a lack of impulse control—before we can build a customized plan.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-primary-navy mt-12 mb-6">
          Beyond Basic Obedience: The Balanced Approach
        </h2>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          At Good Doggos, I don’t just train commands; I shift mindsets. With 8 years of experience tackling the cases other trainers won’t touch, I understand that behavior modification requires a nuanced, balanced methodology. I'm not here just to give a cookie for being "good"—I'm here to show your dog how to be calm. 
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          My foundation as a behaviorist is shaped by a personal trauma. After being attacked by a dog as a child in Mexico, I spent years in fear. Overcoming that trauma required me to master dog behavior and realize that barks and growls are signals that can be managed through leadership. I don't see "mean" dogs; I see dogs in need of "Balanced Clarity."
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          I use high-value rewards and verbal praise to build a relationship of trust, but I also believe in the "fair" side of the equation. This means using calibrated leash corrections to provide clear boundaries. If your dog is charging the fence at Hiram Deville Park, they need to know that behavior is not an option before they can learn what the right choice actually is.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          Whether we are working in the San Jacinto heat or navigating State Street, our goal is real-world reliability. I look at the "why"—is it fear, dominance, or a lack of impulse control? I then build a customized plan for your lifestyle. I don't just work with the dog; I coach you to be the leader your dog is looking for.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6 font-bold">
          Stop settling for a "problem dog" and start building a partnership. Apply for a Free Behavioral Assessment.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
     CTA BAND
══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="relative overflow-hidden bg-[#FBF1E9]" style="border-top: 1px solid #E6DAC6;">
  <div class="w-full h-[3px]" style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #0F6D72, #D1B27F, #0F6D72);"></div>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-20 md:py-24 text-center">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-bold tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color: rgba(15,109,114,0.60);">Your Dog Is Next</p>
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-4" style="color: #0B2744;">
      Ready to See What's Possible?<br/>
      <span class="headline-accent" style="color: #D1B27F; font-style: italic; font-weight: 700;">Start With a Free Assessment.</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="text-base mb-10 max-w-lg mx-auto" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.60);">
      Tell us about your dog. We'll do an honest assessment and point you toward the right program — or tell you if we're not the right fit.
    </p>
    <a href="/apply"
       class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 font-bold text-sm tracking-widest uppercase rounded-full transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5"
       style="background: #D1B27F; color: #0B2744; padding: 18px 44px; box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(209,178,127,0.35);">
      Apply for Free Behavioral Assessment →
    </a>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.40);">Takes less than 3 minutes · No commitment required</p>
  </div>
</div>
</Layout>
